    {
      "sectionId": "section-druid-cantrip-options",
      "parentSectionId": "section-spell-sniper-spell-options",
      "heading": "Druid Cantrip Options",
      "sourceAnchor": "druid-cantrip-options",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-druid-cantrip-options-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Druid’s spells are potential options for clerics and for rangers who take\n\tFighting Style (Druidic Warrior). For the Cleric, Thorn Whip is basically the\n\tonly option worth having. For the Ranger, you can already get all of these\n\tspells and the ability to ignore partial cover with them is so situational\n\tthat there is basically no reason to consider it a benefit."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-druid-cantrip-options-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Magic Stone"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": ": I honestly have no idea if this qualifies, but I think that it would\n\t\t\tbecause it doesn’t actually do anything interesting unless an attack is\n\t\t\tmade. Even if it does, it’s not a good choice.",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "Primal Savagery",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "XGtE",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": If you can add damage to your weapon attacks from basically any source\n\t\tbeyond your ability modifier (Divine Strike, Hunter’s Mark, etc.) your\n\t\tweapon attacks will probably outpace Primal Savagery until high levels."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Produce Flame"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Sacred Flame is considerably better, and if Sacred Flame is available to\n\t\tyou I wouldn’t both with Produce Flame."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Thorn Whip"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": The pull effect is nice."
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
          "itemKinds": [
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered",
            "unordered"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "section-sorcerer-cantrip-options",
      "parentSectionId": "section-spell-sniper-spell-options",
      "heading": "Sorcerer Cantrip Options",
      "sourceAnchor": "sorcerer-cantrip-options",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-sorcerer-cantrip-options-1",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Sorcerer gets access to Fire Bolt and Ray of Frost, neither of which are\n\tavailable to the Bard or the Warlock, but otherwise the Sorcerer’s options\n\toverlap with the Warlock."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "blockId": "block-section-sorcerer-cantrip-options-2",
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": false,
          "items": [
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Booming Blade"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "SCAG / TCoE",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Why would you take Spell Sniper to take a melee cantrip?"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Chill Touch"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Too situational to justify taking this over a more reliable high-damage\n\t\tcantrip."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Fire Bolt"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "PHB",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Simple, reliable damage at range. The only problem is that fire\n\t\tresistance is common. But since the Bard is the only one who might\n\t\treasonably take this and Eldritch Blast is an option, this appeals to\n\t\tliterally no one."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Green-Flame Blade"
              },
              {
                "type": "link",
                "text": "SCAG / TCoE",
                "href": "https://rpgbot.net/dnd5/abbreviations/"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Why would you take Spell Sniper to take a melee cantrip?"
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Ray of Frost"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Fine dmaage and a passable\n\t\tdebuff."
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Shocking Grasp"
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ": Why would you take Spell\n\t\tSniper to take a melee cantrip?"
              }
            ]
          ],
          "depths": [
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0,
            0
          ],
